  "id": "1508350a-103b-5df9-b0ad-b71bde4a0620",
  "slug": "dot-cake-donuts-recipe-11991676",
  "name": "Dot Cake Donuts",
  "recipe_type": "dessert",
  "brief_description": "These playful dot cake donuts transform Hawaiian rolls into an easy shortcut treat with all the nostalgic flavor of a bakery-style sprinkle donut. Crisp on the outside and soft inside, they're filled with creamy vanilla pudding, then topped with sweet frosting and crunchy rainbow sprinkles for a fun new twist on the dot cake trend.",
  "cuisine": "American",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (180 degrees C). Brush rolls with melted butter on all sides and place on a baking sheet."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "Bake in the preheated oven until lightly browned and toasted, 8 to 10 minutes. Set aside to cool slightly, about 5 minutes."
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "text": "While rolls bake, whisk pudding mix, milk, vanilla, and salt together in a bowl until well combined and thickened, about 2 minutes. Refrigerate, uncovered, for 10 minutes to set up."
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "text": "Transfer filling to a piping bag or a plastic bag. Make a small cut in the corner if using a plastic bag."
    },
    {
      "position": 5,
      "text": "Use a paring knife to make a small cut into one side of each roll. Push knife up and around to create an about 3/4-inch square opening without going all the way through. Fill each hole with about 1 1/2 tablespoons filling."
    },
    {
      "position": 6,
      "text": "Spread frosting evenly over tops of filled donuts, about 4 teaspoons each. Place sprinkles in a medium bowl. Dip top of each filled roll in sprinkles, ensuring frosting is fully covered by sprinkles. Serve immediately. Recipe developed by Melissa Gray-Streett"
    }
  ],
  "servings": 12,
  "cooking_time_minutes": 10,
